WEBVTT

1
00:00:07.112 --> 00:00:15.439
do you mean, Henry?"

2
00:00:15.759 --> 00:00:17.040
Cole looked confused.

3
00:00:17.060 --> 00:00:19.542
"We just solved the case!

4
00:00:20.503 --> 00:00:23.746
Nora was sneaking out here to drink soda!"

5
00:00:25.327 --> 00:00:27.649
"Nora confessed," Maggie agreed.

6
00:00:27.669 --> 00:00:31.172
"We should be happy that she didn't argue for once."

7
00:00:32.340 --> 00:00:33.481
"But that's just it."

8
00:00:34.602 --> 00:00:38.084
The more Henry thought about it, the more certain he was that he was right.

9
00:00:38.104 --> 00:00:42.406
"Since when does Nora give up so easily?"

10
00:00:42.426 --> 00:00:44.808
"It does seem strange."

11
00:00:45.208 --> 00:00:46.049
Nathan frowned.

12
00:00:46.069 --> 00:00:48.490
"But she does love soda.

13
00:00:49.471 --> 00:00:50.731
And we caught her in the act."

14
00:00:51.992 --> 00:00:52.493
"Did we?"

15
00:00:52.853 --> 00:00:54.094
Henry looked at each of them.

16
00:00:54.114 --> 00:00:57.716
"Or is Nora even sneakier than we thought?

17
00:00:58.832 --> 00:01:02.934
Maybe she saw us go up in the tree house so she sneaked past on purpose."

18
00:01:04.355 --> 00:01:05.496
"Why would she do that?"

19
00:01:05.836 --> 00:01:06.636
Maggie asked.

20
00:01:07.697 --> 00:01:08.457
Henry shrugged.

21
00:01:08.477 --> 00:01:11.339
"To make us think we'd solved the case.

22
00:01:12.500 --> 00:01:17.963
That way, once we stop paying attention to her, she can go back to doing whatever she's really

23
00:01:18.043 --> 00:01:23.166
doing." "But Nathan said she's not allowed to drink soda," Maggie said.

24
00:01:24.186 --> 00:01:27.288
"So it makes sense that she'd sneak around for something like that.

25
00:01:28.800 --> 00:01:32.403
Remember how she sneaked an extra cup of lemonade from my stand?"

26
00:01:32.423 --> 00:01:34.945
"Yes," Henry said.

27
00:01:34.965 --> 00:01:37.928
"But this still doesn't make sense to me.

28
00:01:38.969 --> 00:01:42.091
Why would she hide the soda this far from her house?"

29
00:01:43.212 --> 00:01:46.015
"So her parents wouldn't find it," Cole said.

30
00:01:46.035 --> 00:01:47.896
"That's obvious."

31
00:01:48.417 --> 00:01:49.457
Henry shook his head.

32
00:01:49.478 --> 00:01:52.720
"There are tons of closer hiding places."

33
00:01:52.740 --> 00:01:55.102
"I guess so."

34
00:01:56.003 --> 00:01:56.904
Maggie looked around.

35
00:01:58.764 --> 00:02:00.885
"But this shed is a pretty good spot.

36
00:02:01.825 --> 00:02:05.887
She could sit inside and drink the soda, and nobody would ever see her."

37
00:02:06.987 --> 00:02:08.048
Nathan frowned again.

38
00:02:08.068 --> 00:02:12.350
"Now that I think about it, she hates places like this shed."

39
00:02:14.050 --> 00:02:15.071
He stepped inside.

40
00:02:15.091 --> 00:02:21.173
"It's dark in here, and there are a ton of spiders and other bugs.

41
00:02:22.894 --> 00:02:24.395
Nora does not like bugs!"

42
00:02:26.315 --> 00:02:28.633
"I forgot about that," Maggie said.

43
00:02:28.653 --> 00:02:34.678
"When she bought lemonade from me, she double-checked to make sure there were no bugs in it."

44
00:02:35.139 --> 00:02:35.759
She shrugged.

45
00:02:35.779 --> 00:02:37.581
"But so what?

46
00:02:38.622 --> 00:02:41.664
Maybe she decided soda was more important than bugs."

47
00:02:41.684 --> 00:02:44.347
"Maybe," Henry said.

48
00:02:45.327 --> 00:02:48.630
They started walking through the woods, still talking about the case.

49
00:02:54.304 --> 00:02:58.347
"But why would she sneak out after her bedtime just to drink soda?

50
00:02:59.388 --> 00:03:01.609
She could do it just as easily during the day."

51
00:03:01.629 --> 00:03:05.932
"I guess that's true," Nathan agreed, looking thoughtful.

52
00:03:07.173 --> 00:03:08.814
Maggie still didn't look convinced.

53
00:03:08.834 --> 00:03:13.217
"We already know that Nora is weird," she said.

54
00:03:13.237 --> 00:03:16.019
"Nothing she does makes a lot of sense."

55
00:03:16.039 --> 00:03:22.224
"It does seem strange that there are only four empty cans in the shed," said Cole.

56
00:03:23.308 --> 00:03:24.909
"How many times has she sneaked out?"

57
00:03:24.929 --> 00:03:28.412
"More than four times," Nathan said.

58
00:03:29.593 --> 00:03:32.515
Henry could tell that his friends were starting to believe him.

59
00:03:32.535 --> 00:03:39.680
"Also, when we saw her sneaking out yesterday, she wasn't heading toward the Smiths' yard," he said.

60
00:03:39.700 --> 00:03:46.725
"Remember? She was walking straight past the tree house toward the back of her own yard."

61
00:03:46.745 --> 00:03:48.586
"You're right!"

62
00:03:49.087 --> 00:03:50.368
Maggie's eyes widened.

63
00:03:51.340 --> 00:03:54.381
"Do you really think she tricked us into following her here?"

64
00:03:54.401 --> 00:03:56.062
"But why?"

65
00:03:56.462 --> 00:03:58.263
Cole looked more confused than ever.

66
00:03:58.283 --> 00:04:00.504
"What's she really doing?"

67
00:04:00.524 --> 00:04:06.807
"That's what we still have to figure out before we accept Nathan's money," Henry said.

68
00:04:07.908 --> 00:04:09.108
Maggie sighed loudly.

69
00:04:09.128 --> 00:04:12.710
"Maybe you're right," she told Henry.

70
00:04:12.730 --> 00:04:16.872
"Mom says you're the most logical person she knows.

71
00:04:18.044 --> 00:04:21.365
And Nora is definitely the sneakiest kid in the neighborhood.

72
00:04:22.406 --> 00:04:24.367
We should make sure she's not tricking us."

73
00:04:24.387 --> 00:04:27.228
"Yeah," Cole agreed.

74
00:04:27.248 --> 00:04:28.729
"But how?"

75
00:04:28.749 --> 00:04:31.670
"Good question," Nathan said.

76
00:04:32.730 --> 00:04:34.471
They all turned to look at Henry.

77
00:04:35.451 --> 00:04:36.152
He smiled.

78
00:04:37.092 --> 00:04:38.993
"Nora is sneaky," he said.

79
00:04:39.013 --> 00:04:43.375
"That means we have to be sneakier than she is."

80
00:04:43.395 --> 00:04:46.316
"Okay," Cole said.

81
00:04:47.388 --> 00:04:47.948
"But how?"

82
00:04:48.909 --> 00:04:50.350
Henry thought for a second.

83
00:04:51.110 --> 00:04:56.553
The bad news was that they still had no idea what Nora was really doing when she sneaked

84
00:04:56.693 --> 00:04:59.935
out. Their investigation had failed so far.

85
00:05:00.955 --> 00:05:03.617
But the good news was that Nora thought she'd tricked them.

86
00:05:04.717 --> 00:05:08.479
She wouldn't expect them to keep investigating after they'd solved the case.

87
00:05:09.960 --> 00:05:13.322
That meant she wouldn't be as careful next time she sneaked out.

88
00:05:13.342 --> 00:05:16.844
"I have a plan," Henry told his friends.

89
00:05:17.972 --> 00:05:19.994
"It's time for another stakeout."

90
00:05:21.255 --> 00:05:22.116
Maggie groaned.

91
00:05:23.517 --> 00:05:25.238
"Again?" she said.

92
00:05:25.258 --> 00:05:29.222
"But my favorite horse show is on TV tonight!

93
00:05:30.342 --> 00:05:34.686
I don't want to miss it, especially since it seems like I'll never earn enough money for riding

94
00:05:34.746 --> 00:05:40.631
lessons!" "You'll have enough money before long, Maggie," Henry said, smiling.

95
00:05:40.651 --> 00:05:43.894
"And you can record your show and watch it later.

96
00:05:44.895 --> 00:05:46.316
It'll be worth missing it tonight."

97
00:05:47.284 --> 00:05:48.564
Cole looked doubtful.

98
00:05:48.584 --> 00:05:50.365
"Are you sure?"

99
00:05:50.745 --> 00:05:51.245
he said.

100
00:05:51.265 --> 00:05:57.067
"Even if Nora thinks we gave up, she'll still be sneaking around so her parents don't catch her.

101
00:05:58.707 --> 00:06:01.028
How are we supposed to follow her without being seen?"

102
00:06:02.408 --> 00:06:04.129
"Don't worry," Henry said.

103
00:06:04.149 --> 00:06:06.489
"I told you I have a plan.

104
00:06:07.469 --> 00:06:10.130
This isn't going to be an ordinary stakeout."

105
00:06:10.150 --> 00:06:12.051
"What do you mean?"

106
00:06:12.491 --> 00:06:13.251
Nathan asked.

107
00:06:14.371 --> 00:06:15.091
Henry winked.

108
00:06:16.172 --> 00:06:21.487
"This time our stakeout is going to have an extra-special, detective twist!"
